# Goal
Add a "Week" section to group lessons by week in the curriculum. This will involve adding a "Week Number" field to lessons, allowing instructors to organize their curriculum into weeks instead of just individual days.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The lessons will be grouped by their assigned Week Number. Do you want lessons inside each week to still use the "Day Number (Sort Order)" for ordering within that week?
> For example:
> - **Week 1**
>   - Day 1: Introduction
>   - Day 2: Setup
> - **Week 2**
>   - Day 1: Advanced Topics (or Day 3 if you prefer continuous numbering)

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Database Schema
#### [NEW] `supabase/migrations/015_add_week_to_lessons.sql`
- Add an `ALTER TABLE lessons ADD COLUMN week_number INTEGER DEFAULT 1;` script to persist the change.
- A quick Node.js script will be run to immediately apply this to your active database.

### 2. Type Definitions
#### [MODIFY] `src/types/database.ts`
- Update the `Lesson` interface to include the new `week_number: number` property.

### 3. Server Actions
#### [MODIFY] `src/features/admin/actions/builder-actions.ts`
- Update `addLesson` and `updateLesson` functions to extract `week_number` from the form data and save it to the database.

### 4. Instructor View (Curriculum Builder)
#### [MODIFY] `src/features/admin/components/CurriculumBuilder.tsx`
- Add `week_number` to the `EditingItem` interface.
- Add a new `Input` field for "Week Number" in the Add/Edit Lesson modal (defaulting to 1).
- Refactor the display logic to group `lessons` by `week_number`. Render a distinct header for each week, containing the lessons belonging to that week.

### 5. Student View (Course Dashboard)
#### [MODIFY] `src/app/(dashboard)/courses/[courseId]/page.tsx`
- Refactor the curriculum list to group lessons by `week_number` so students see a structured weekly schedule.
- Update CSS styling if necessary to distinguish week headers.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- Go to the instructor builder and add a lesson, setting Week = 1 and Day = 1.
- Add another lesson, setting Week = 2 and Day = 1.
- Verify that the builder groups them under "Week 1" and "Week 2" headers.
- Switch to the student view (`/courses/[courseId]`) and verify that the curriculum displays the lessons grouped by week.
